{title: Softly and Tenderly}
{title_ko: 예수가 우리를 부르는 소리}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 528장}
{artist: Will L. Thompson}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: Eb}
{key_original: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Softly and tenderly Jesus is [Bb7]calling
[Bb7]Calling for you and for [Eb]me
[Eb]See, on the portals He's [Ab]waiting and [Eb]watching
[Eb]Watching for [Bb7]you and for [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb]Come home, come home
[Ab]Ye who are [Eb]weary, come [Bb7]home
[Eb]Earnestly, tenderly, [Ab]Jesus is [Eb]calling
[Eb]Calling, O [Bb7]sinner, come [Eb]home
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Why should we tarry when Jesus is [Bb7]pleading
[Bb7]Pleading for you and for [Eb]me
[Eb]Why should we linger and [Ab]heed not His [Eb]mercies
[Eb]Mercies for [Bb7]you and for [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Time is now fleeting, the moments are [Bb7]passing
[Bb7]Passing from you and from [Eb]me
[Eb]Shadows are gathering, [Ab]deathbeds are [Eb]coming
[Eb]Coming for [Bb7]you and for [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
